04325536686959308,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":92.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.0047299997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Huntington Ingalls Industries, Inc. designs, builds, overhauls, and repairs military ships in the United States. It operates through three segments: Ingalls, Newport News, and Mission Technologies. The company is involved in the design and construction of non-nuclear ships comprising amphibious assault ships, surface combatants, and national security cutters for the U.S. Navy and U.S. Coast Guard. It also provides nuclear-powered ships, such as aircraft carriers and submarines, as well as refueling and overhaul, and inactivation services of nuclear-powered aircraft carriers. In addition, the company offers naval nuclear support services, including fleet services comprising design, construction, maintenance, and disposal activities for in-service the U.S. Navy nuclear ships; and maintenance services on nuclear reactor prototypes. Further, the company provides C5ISR systems and operations; application of artificial intelligence and machine learning to battlefield decisions; defensive and offensive cyberspace strategies and electronic warfare; uncrewed autonomous systems; live, virtual, and constructive solutions; platform modernization; and critical nuclear operations. The company has a strategic partnership with HD Hyundai Heavy Industries to implement intelligent mechanized welding systems at Huntington Ingalls Industries, Inc.'s Ingalls Shipbuilding division. Huntington Ingalls Industries, Inc. was founded in 1886 and is headquartered in Newport News, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher Douglas Kastner | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 46K people. Revenue per employee of $271K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 16\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Huntington Ingalls Industries,  is a large-cap industrials business with a $12.1B market cap on $12.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $794M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.98\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 6.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4487582.7},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 28% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (HII) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_HII_That_Institutions_Follow_111126054601_1794437161.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794437161.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alembic Global Advisors Estimates HII Q4 Earnings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/alembic-global-advisors-estimates-hii-q4-earnings.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794400183.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Path Robotics Raises $300M for AI Welding Robots; HII's $900M Navy Ceiling Has No Disclosed Split","source":"techtimes.com","link":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/330439/20261111/path-robotics-raise